.TH SOX-QUALITY 1 "November 13, 2026" "SoX" "Sound eXchange"
.SH NAME
sox-quality \- produce a JSON audio quality report
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sox-quality
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIfile\fR|\fIdirectory\fR ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sox-quality
opens one or more audio files with libSoX and writes a machine-readable
JSON report.  Metrics include integrated loudness, maximum short-term
loudness, true peak, clipped samples, DC offset and an estimated noise floor.
.PP
When a directory is given, it is scanned recursively by default.  Files are
analyzed independently and a batch summary is generated.  The summary's
integrated loudness is calculated over the union of all 400 ms gating blocks
from successfully analyzed files; it is not an average of the per-file LUFS
values.  Other summary metrics are maxima or sums as indicated by their names.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
.TQ
.BI \-\-output= file
Write JSON to
.I file
instead of standard output.  A
.I file
of
.B -
means standard output.
.TP
.B \-r
.TQ
.B \-\-recursive
Recurse into directories.  This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-recursive
Analyze only files directly contained in directories.
.TP
.BI \-\-absolute\-gate= lufs
Set the EBU R128 absolute gate.  The default is
.B \-70 LUFS
and accepted values are in
[\-120, 0).
.TP
.BI \-\-relative\-gate= lu
Set the EBU R128 relative gate below the absolute-gated mean.  The default is
.B 10 LU
and accepted values are in
(0, 40].
.TP
.B \-q
.TQ
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress libSoX warning and error messages.  The JSON still contains an
.B error
entry for files that could not be analyzed.
.TP
.B \-h
.TQ
.B \-\-help
Display command usage.
.TP
.B \-V
.TQ
.B \-\-version
Display the libSoX version.
.SH ANALYSIS
The default calculations implement ITU-R BS.1770-4 and EBU R128 as follows.
.SS Loudness
K-weighting is derived for the actual sample rate using the BS.1770 pre-filter
(high shelf) and RLB high-pass filter.  Input is grouped into 100 ms bins
rounded to the nearest sample.  Integrated loudness uses 400 ms blocks, i.e.
four bins, advanced by one bin, for 75% overlap.
.PP
The absolute gate accepts blocks at or above
.B \-70 LUFS.
The relative gate is
.B 10 LU
below the mean energy of the absolute-gated blocks.  Integrated loudness is
computed from the gated blocks at or above both thresholds.  Short-term
loudness uses a sliding 3000 ms window advanced every 100 ms, and the report
contains its maximum.  Complete windows only are used; a file shorter than
400 ms has no integrated loudness, and one shorter than 3 seconds has no
short-term maximum.
.PP
Channel weights follow BS.1770: 1.0 for the first three channels, 1.41 for
surround channels, and zero for the LFE channel in layouts of six or more
channels.  For four channels the weights are 1.0, 1.0, 1.41, 1.41; for five
channels they are 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.41, 1.41.  All weights are 1.0 for mono and
stereo.  Channels beyond six are excluded because SoX does not expose channel
layout metadata to this command.
.SS True peak
True peak is measured on the unweighted signal using 4-times oversampling with
a 49-tap Hanning-windowed sinc polyphase interpolator and is reported in dBTP.
.SS Clipping
A clipped sample is a decoded sample equal to the positive or negative
full-scale code of the source precision.  Decoder-reported out-of-range
conversions are included as well.  The value is a sample count, not a count of
runs.
.SS DC offset
.B dc_offset
is the arithmetic mean of all decoded samples across all channels, normalized
to the internal
[\-1, 1)
range.
.B dc_offset_dbfs
is
20 log10(|dc_offset|).
.SS Noise floor
.B noise_floor_dbfs
is a non-normative estimate: the 10th percentile (nearest rank) of complete
400 ms unweighted RMS blocks, expressed in dBFS.  It is useful as a batch
outlier check, but it is not an EBU R128 defined metric.
.SH OUTPUT
The output is one JSON object.  Its top-level fields are:
.TP
.B schema_version
Integer schema version, currently 1.
.TP
.B report
Always
.BR sox-quality .
.TP
.B tool
Object containing the tool name and libSoX version.
.TP
.B generated_at
UTC timestamp in ISO 8601 form.
.TP
.B mode
.B single
or
.BR batch .
.TP
.B method
The active windows, thresholds and algorithm descriptions.
.TP
.B summary
Aggregate metrics, file counts and total duration.  Unavailable numeric
metrics are represented as JSON
.BR null .
.TP
.B files
Array of per-file objects.  Successful entries contain
.B format
and
.B metrics
objects; failed entries contain
.B status: "error"
and an
.B error
message.
.PP
The per-file
.B metrics
object has the following numeric fields:
.B integrated_loudness_lufs
(LUFS),
.B short_term_loudness_max_lufs
(LUFS),
.B true_peak_dbtp
(dBTP),
.B clipped_samples
(integer count),
.B dc_offset
(normalized linear mean),
.B dc_offset_dbfs
(dBFS), and
.B noise_floor_dbfs
(dBFS).
.PP
The batch
.B summary
also contains
.B files_total,
.B files_analyzed,
.B files_failed,
.B files_with_clipping,
.B duration_seconds
and
.BR scalar_samples .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero if all attempted files were analyzed successfully.  Non-zero if any file
could not be opened or analyzed, or if the JSON output could not be written.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate a report for one file:
.EX
  sox-quality master.wav > master-quality.json
.EE
Generate a report and summary for a delivery directory:
.EX
  sox-quality -o delivery-quality.json delivery/
.EE
Use the same integrated-loudness measurement as FFmpeg's loudnorm filter for
cross-checking:
.EX
  ffmpeg -i master.wav -af loudnorm=I=-23:print_format=json -f null -
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.B sox(1),
.B soxi(1),
.B soxformat(7),
.B libsox(3)
